config V4L2_LOOPBACK
	tristate "v4l2loopback: virtual video loopback devices"
	depends on VIDEO_DEV
	help
	  v4l2loopback (https://github.com/v4l2loopback/v4l2loopback, v0.15.4)
	  creates virtual video devices: frames written to the output side of
	  a device (e.g. by a camera pipeline) are read by applications from
	  its capture side, as from a real camera.

	  To compile this driver as a module, choose M here: the module will
	  be called v4l2loopback.
